      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the sum of all \\( x \\) that satisfy the equation \\( f^{-1}(x) = f((2x)^{-1}) \\) for the given function \\( f(x) = 16x + 3 \\).\n\n### Step 1: Find the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\)\n\nThe function given is \\( f(x) = 16x + 3 \\). To find the inverse, we start by setting \\( y = f(x) \\):\n\n\\[ y = 16x + 3 \\]\n\nNext, solve for \\( x \\) in terms of \\( y \\):\n\n\\[ y - 3 = 16x \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{y - 3}{16} \\]\n\nThus, the inverse function is:\n\n\\[ f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x - 3}{16} \\]\n\n### Step 2: Substitute \\( f((2x)^{-1}) \\) into the inverse function\n\nWe need to evaluate \\( f((2x)^{-1}) \\):\n\n\\[ f((2x)^{-1}) = f\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right) \\]\n\nUsing the original function \\( f(x) = 16x + 3 \\), we substitute \\( \\frac{1}{2x} \\) for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[ f\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right) = 16 \\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right) + 3 \\]\n\\[ f\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right) = \\frac{16}{2x} + 3 \\]\n\\[ f\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right) = \\frac{8}{x} + 3 \\]\n\n### Step 3: Set up the equation \\( f^{-1}(x) = f((2x)^{-1}) \\)\n\nNow, we set the inverse function equal to the evaluated function:\n\n\\[ f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x - 3}{16} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{x - 3}{16} = \\frac{8}{x} + 3 \\]\n\n### Step 4: Solve the equation\n\nFirst, clear the fractions by multiplying every term by \\( 16x \\):\n\n\\[ x(x - 3) = 16(8) + 3(16x) \\]\n\\[ x^2 - 3x = 128 + 48x \\]\n\nRearrange all terms to one side of the equation:\n\n\\[ x^2 - 3x - 48x - 128 = 0 \\]\n\\[ x^2 - 51x - 128 = 0 \\]\n\n### Step 5: Solve the quadratic equation\n\nWe solve the quadratic equation \\( x^2 - 51x - 128 = 0 \\) using the quadratic formula \\( x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = -51 \\), and \\( c = -128 \\):\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{-(-51) \\pm \\sqrt{(-51)^2 - 4(1)(-128)}}{2(1)} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{51 \\pm \\sqrt{2601 + 512}}{2} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{51 \\pm \\sqrt{3113}}{2} \\]\n\n### Step 6: Find the sum of the roots\n\nThe sum of the roots of the quadratic equation \\( ax^2 + bx + c = 0 \\) is given by \\( -\\frac{b}{a} \\). Here, \\( a = 1 \\) and \\( b = -51 \\):\n\n\\[ \\text{Sum of the roots} = -\\frac{-51}{1} = 51 \\]\n\nThus, the sum of all \\( x \\) that satisfy the equation \\( f^{-1}(x) = f((2x)^{-1}) \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{51}\n\\]",
