      "text": "Apeano Solution\n\nGiven $f(x)$ is an exponential function, we can deduce $f^{-1}(x)$ is a logarithmic function. We can take $f(x)$ and $f^{-1}(x)$ in the form of variables $g(x)$ and $h(x)$ for simplicity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{cases}\ng(x) = f(x) & =& 16x + 3 \\\\\nh(x) = f^{-1}(x) & =& \\frac1{16x+3} \\\\\n\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nSince $f(x) = (2x)^{-1}$, we can use logarithms to transfer $x$ to $f(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{align*}\nf^{-1}(x) &= \\frac1{16x + 3}\\\\\n\\therefore f(x) &= f(f^{-1}(x)) = \\frac1{16\\left(\\frac1{16x+3}\\right) + 3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{16x + 27}{3} \\tag{*}\n\\end{align*}\n$$\n\nThe set of $x$ that satisfy $(\\text{*})$ is $\\{\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{3}{4}\\}$, which sum to $\\boxed{\\frac{7}{4}}$",
